  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "R2-R3 already apply temperature-dependent tensile molecular-dynamics simulations to nanowires of the closely related equiatomic CoNiCrFeMn FCC alloy, while R3 identifies partial-dislocation-mediated deformation, twinning, and FCC/HCP structural evolution. R15 independently connects low-temperature deformation of Cantor-family FCC alloys to stacking faults, nanotwins, and HCP-like structures. Together these records make tensile MD on a closely related Fe-Ni-Cr-Mn alloy and plasticity mediated by partial dislocations, stacking faults, and local HCP coordination a plausible proposal. The precise bulk periodic geometry, crystallographic loading directions, strain-rate sweep, vacancy-cluster nucleation, lack of twinning or bulk transformation, and detailed rate-insensitive yield result are not directly anticipated."
